# Orbital Agronomist

Voice hotline for fictional smallholder farmers. Satellite and weather data are real. Each scenario replays a real past event.

## Agent rules

- Work one phase from `docs/PLAN.md` at a time. Stop when its acceptance criteria pass.
- Commit after every task (`feat:`, `fix:`, `data:`, `docs:`). After every task, append one line to `docs/CURSOR_LOG.md`: timestamp, what was built, Cursor feature used.
- Never expose `XAI_API_KEY` or `SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY` to the browser. The browser gets an xAI ephemeral token and the Supabase publishable key only. Privileged calls go through Next.js API routes.
- Config-driven by farm. No farm-specific logic in components. A new farm is an entry in `data/farms.config.json` plus rerunning scripts.
- Do not add dependencies beyond the plan's stack without asking.
- When an xAI API detail is unclear, check https://docs.x.ai (append `.md` to the docs URL). Log unknown server event types in dev.
- User-facing copy stays honest: farmers are fictional; Sentinel-2 and NASA POWER data are real; guidance is general.

## Demo farms

| id | farmer | languages | crop | event | window | baseline |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `cn-rice-2022` | 张师傅 (Master Zhang) | `zh` primary, `en` toggle | Mid-season rice | 2022 Yangtze basin drought + heatwave | 2022-06-01 → 2022-09-30 | 2021, same window |

The demo is this one farm. English is the judge-facing language; Mandarin is the showcase. The field is a rice cluster in Sichuan / Chongqing / Jiangxi. Simulated today is the last cloud-free observation in mid/late August 2022.

Clip topics: `irrigation_timing`, `prioritize_flowering_fields`, `heat_stress_foliar_spray`.

## Data layout

- `data/farms.config.json` — per-farm config (polygon path, windows, languages, profile, clip topics)
- `data/farms/{farmId}/field.geojson` — polygon Allen draws
- `data/farms/{farmId}/farm.json` — built by scripts
- `data/farms/{farmId}/diagnosis.json` — built by Grok
